WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.040
New York State files lawsuit against polymarket alleging illegal gambling operation. This is prediction

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:12.600
market's daily, episode two, journalism and education, never a bet. New York Attorney General

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:19.060
Latisha James and Governor Kathy Hocal filed a lawsuit against polymarket on September 24th,

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:25.120
2026. The complaint alleges the platform operates an illegal gambling business within the state.

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:28.340
The action is a filing, not a final ruling.

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:32.880
Polly Market faces potential enforcement if the court accepts the claims.

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:40.800
Separate reports from CoinGape and WSJ confirm the filing escalates an ongoing state crackdown on prediction markets.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:46.080
The suit names Polly Market directly and seeks to halt operations in New York.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:52.920
Fair Canada CEO Jean-Paul Bouraud stated that prediction market contracts remain wagers

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:55.500
in substance, even if structured as derivatives.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:01:01.120
The group called for keeping current limits unless broader access proves benefits to investors

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:02.280
and the public interest.

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:08.020
The statement covers contracts limited to economic, financial, or climate matters in Canada.

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:13.860
Fair Canada noted disagreement among regulators, financial firms, and academics on whether

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:17.860
sports and entertainment contracts fall under securities or gaming rules.

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:23.780
The Canadian securities administrators ruled last month that sports and entertainment contracts

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:26.240
should stay outside securities legislation.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:31.780
Former New Jersey Governor Chris Christie urged attorneys general across states to pursue

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:34.220
enforcement against prediction market platforms.

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:38.360
The call comes amid multiple state actions filed in recent weeks.

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:43.800
Lawmakers asked the Supreme Court to review the call sheet litigation over event contracts.

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:48.760
The request targets ongoing questions about federal preemption of state gaming laws.

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:55.280
The Washington Post column examined historical precedent from 1591 on attempts to restrict

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:56.300
similar markets.

00:01:56.760 --> 00:02:01.960
It argued that earlier Bands produced enforcement problems without eliminating trading activity.

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:08.300
On the board today, the leading outcome on an early 2028 AI movie generation question

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:16.020
sits at 34.9% yes on Manifold after 41,000 mana changed hands in the last 24 hours.

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:24.500
The superhuman math problem solving question before 2030 without AGI first prices at 86.5%

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:29.160
yes on Manifold after 16,000 mana traded in the same period.

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:36.100
The chance U.S. inflation reaches 5% in 2026 prices at 9% on polymarket.

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:45.480
Average weekly earnings in Canada stand 3.2% higher year over year at $1,347.14 on

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:46.020
CalSHE.

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:53.780
The 2028 Democratic presidential nominee market prices John Assoff at 17% on CalSHE after

00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:57.100
1.4 million contracts traded in 24 hours.

00:02:57.100 --> 00:03:00.820
Access to these venues depends on where the listener lives.

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:05.220
Metaculous launched the AI existential risk explorer tool,

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:08.040
created by director of forecasting Ryan Beck.

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:14.160
The site displays how forecasters assess AI-caused catastrophe and extinction risks.

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:20.100
Dedicated X-risk forecasters on the platform currently price extinction risk at 22%,

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:24.100
while professional forecasters price it at 7.5%.

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:29.580
percent. How it works begins with automated market makers that recruit third party liquidity

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:36.540
providers who deposit assets and earn fees from trades. The archive paper bootstrapping liquidity

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:42.960
in BTC-denominated prediction markets shows cross market making against stablecoin venues supplies

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:49.060
the most user-friendly risk profile yet requires active professional makers or platform subsidies.

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:55.300
The same paper finds DeFi redirection of user trades enables rapid bootstrapping, but

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:59.520
exposes participants to liquidation thresholds and exchange rate volatility.

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:05.420
A general theory of liquidity provisioning for prediction markets demonstrates that protocols

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:10.880
allowing arbitrary cost functions can run multiple market makers in parallel, while

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:14.040
recovering existing DeFi approaches as special cases.

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:20.480
Liquidity expressed as a matrix valued function becomes necessary once three or more securities

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:25.120
trade because single-dimensional parameters cannot cover the full price space.

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:31.000
Thin markets move sharply on single trades because limited depth leaves wide bid-ask spreads

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:32.760
that one order can cross.

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:39.540
Listeners can identify thin markets by low 24-hour volume relative to open interest and

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:43.140
by observing large price jumps after modest trading activity.

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:48.880
The paper's note that automated market making remains simple to deploy but carries capital

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:51.780
inefficiency and permanent loss risk for providers.

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:57.200
Cross market making trades stability for the need for ongoing professional oversight.

